        "statement": "Use the selected classical pure $SU(2)$ gauge model on oriented and time-oriented Minkowski $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, one selected smooth right-principal bundle $P\\to M$, connection $A$, curvature $F_A=dA+\\tfrac12[A\\wedge A]$, invariant form $\\kappa(X,Y)=-2\\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$, and positive dimensionless $g_{\\mathrm{YM}}$ from the non-Abelian Yang–Mills model. Use natural units $\\hbar=c=1$, so $[x^\\mu]=-1$, $[g_{\\mathrm{YM}}]=0$, $[A_\\mu]=1$, and $[F_{A,\\mu\\nu}]=2$. Let $g=g_{\\mathrm{YM}}$.\n\nChoose a finite index set $I$ with $|I|\\geq1$. For each $a\\in I$, choose a finite-dimensional complex Hermitian space $V_a$, a smooth unitary representation $R_a:SU(2)\\to U(V_a)$, and its associated vector bundle $E_a=P\\times_{R_a}V_a$. The matter field $\\Phi^a$ is a smooth chiral superfield with local components in $E_a$ and unique scalar, left Weyl, and complex auxiliary components $(\\phi^a,\\psi^a,F^a)$; their engineering dimensions are $1$, $3/2$, and $2$. Let $V$ be the full real vector prepotential of the local vector-superfield definition, with connection-normalized component $A_\\mu=-ig B_\\mu$ in a local unitary frame, and let $\\mathcal W_\\alpha$ be its abstract connection-normalized Lie-algebra-valued chiral field strength. Its represented matrix curvature is $\\mathscr C_{\\alpha,R}=-\\tfrac14\\bar D^2(e^{-2gV_R}D_\\alpha e^{2gV_R})$; the dictionary is $\\rho_{R*}(\\mathcal W_\\alpha)=\\mathscr C_{\\alpha,R}/(2i)$, so in the defining representation $\\kappa_{\\mathbb C}(\\mathcal W^\\alpha,\\mathcal W_\\alpha)=\\operatorname{Tr}_2(\\mathscr C^\\alpha\\mathscr C_\\alpha)/2$. The matter covariant derivative is $D_\\mu\\phi^a=\\partial_\\mu\\phi^a+\\rho_{a*}(A_\\mu)\\phi^a=\\partial_\\mu\\phi^a-ig B_\\mu^b t_{b,a}\\phi^a$, where $t_{b,a}=i\\rho_{a*}(T_b)$ and $T_b=-i\\sigma_b/2$. Take smooth field-dependent component fluctuations with compact support in the local trivializing regions